+## LvlLimitBoostr
+
+- **What it does**: +1 to a party Digimon's level limit (`maxLevel`). Only for a Digimon at
+  its limit whose limit is below 99; a limit of 99 can't be raised.
+- **Where it comes from** (with mystery encounters on; `FP_BOOST_PCT`, 1 %):
+  - 1 % of won ? battles: offered right after the battle (`Stg40_FpNoteBattle` at the
+    encounter, the battle stage's win path notes the win, `Stg40_FpBattleBoostDue` back in the
+    dungeon). None loses it.
+  - 1 % of floors with a ? party: one of the floor's chests holds it instead of its item
+    (`Stg40_FpRollChestBoost` after `Stg40_SpawnChests`). None leaves it in the chest, which
+    stays closed (as with a full bag), to come back to.
+- **The prompt** (`Stg40_FpBoostPrompt`): a message box with the title, the selected party
+  Digimon (name, level / limit) or None, and a hint; Up / Down (or Left / Right) choose,
+  (X) confirms, (O) is None. A Digimon that can't take it says why. The text is the game's own
+  glyph encoding (`Stg40_FpGlyphs`, the table of `host/devedit.c`).
+- **Never in the bag**: used at once or left, so a save stays readable by the official port.
+
